PRO-FORMA FIRST BOARD OF DIRECTORS RESOLUTION OF YUHANGHOESA (유한회사) — ADOPTED BY UNANIMOUS WRITTEN CONSENT IN LIEU OF A MEETING.

RESOLVED, that the incorporation of Yuhan Hoesa (the 'Company') under the Commercial Act of the Republic of Korea has been duly completed as evidenced by the Certificate of Incorporation registered with the Commercial Registry Division of the [Name of District Court] on [Date of Registration], Registration No. [Registration Number];

RESOLVED FURTHER, that the paid-in capital of the Company in the amount of KRW [Amount] has been duly deposited into the Company's escrow account and released to the Company's operating account No. [Account Number] maintained at [Bank Name], and that such amount is recorded in the Company's books as issued and outstanding capital stock, fully paid and non-assessable;

RESOLVED FURTHER, that the registered office of the Company is hereby fixed and adopted at [Full Street Address, Korean Postal Code, City, South Korea], and the Company authorizes the Chief Executive Officer or any Director to execute a lease agreement for such premises, to file notices of change of registered office if required, and to perform all acts necessary to maintain the Company's registered address with the court registry;

RESOLVED FURTHER, that the banking relationship of the Company is established and the following persons are designated as authorized signatories for all bank accounts: [Name and Title of CEO], [Name and Title of CFO], and [Name and Title of Director]; provided that any two authorized signatures shall be required for all transactions exceeding USD 50,000 or the KRW equivalent, and any one signature for transactions below such threshold; the banking authorization includes the authority to open, operate, close, and pledge accounts, to negotiate and deposit checks, notes, and drafts, to borrow money, to issue loans, to purchase foreign exchange, and to execute any bank agreements or guarantees on behalf of the Company;

RESOLVED FURTHER, that the following officers are appointed: [Name], Chief Executive Officer; [Name], Chief Financial Officer; [Name], Company Secretary; and [Name], Compliance Officer, each to serve at the pleasure of the Board of Directors for a term of one year;

RESOLVED FURTHER, that the Company adopts its corporate seal (법인인감) and registered seal (인감) with the competent registry, and the Company authorizes the CEO to keep custody of the seal and to use it for all statutory and commercial purposes;

RESOLVED FURTHER, that the Company hereby adopts the initial fiscal year ending December 31 of each calendar year and authorizes the CEO to retain an external licensed accountant (공인회계사) for the preparation of annual financial statements and the execution of the annual external audit if required under the Act on External Audit of Stock Companies (주식회사 등의 외부감사에 관한 법률);

RESOLVED FURTHER, that the Company authorizes and directs the CEO, CFO, and Company Secretary to take all necessary or convenient actions to open accounts with Stripe Billing and Mercury ACH, to register the Company for Korean Value-Added Tax under Article 5 of the Value-Added Tax Act, to obtain a business registration certificate (사업자등록증) from the National Tax Service (국세청), and to carry out any other corporate housekeeping or regulatory filings as may be necessary for the business purpose of providing developer infrastructure, database, API monitoring and DevOps cloud tools.

This resolution (the 'Pro-Forma First Board Resolution') was adopted by unanimous written consent of all directors on [Date], and remains in full force and effect unless amended or rescinded by a subsequent board resolution. Certified this [Day] day of [Month], [Year].
